WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.120 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
Buffer separates provider reads, normalized snapshots, and scenario

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:08.300 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
calculations. Public account lookup needs no wallet connection.

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:11.380 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
The optional wallet picker supplies an address;

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:13.660 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
Buffer does not submit trades.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:17.360 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
Here, Velocity is selected on Solana mainnet.

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:21.640 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
The server checks account ownership, market identity, and oracle

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:24.500 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
validity before exposing an eligible observation.

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:29.140 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
Account identity, source slots, and timestamps remain inspectable.

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:33.540 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
A stale or failed refresh withholds calculations and exports

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:35.480 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
until a valid replacement arrives.

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:39.380 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
For a supported linear position, the price effect is

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:43.400 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
signed quantity, times frozen price, times the selected shock.

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:47.420 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
Decimal arithmetic preserves exact report values.

00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:49.560 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
Quote currencies remain separate.

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:54.720 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
This calculation excludes funding, fees, future fills, and collateral

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:58.800 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
price changes. Current maintenance collateral and requirement come

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:00.160 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
from the Velocity observation.

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:02.300 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
Their difference is headroom.

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:06.640 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
A separate liquidation model changes one position's price while

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:08.160 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
holding the other prices fixed.

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:11.080 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
Its assumptions and exclusions are visible;

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:13.720 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
it is not the protocol's liquidation engine.

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:18.000 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
Pacifica supports price scenarios with API timestamps.

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:22.460 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
Jupiter remains inventory only, and legacy Drift is paused.

00:01:22.460 --> 00:01:27.360 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
Devnet observations are clearly identified as test values and

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:29.100 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
never enter background monitoring.

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:33.380 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
Mainnet and devnet reports retain their network identity.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:36.900 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
Hosted rules can watch maintenance headroom or a market's

00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:41.420 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
liquidation distance. Owner scoped storage, fresh checks, and a

00:01:41.420 --> 00:01:43.400 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
durable outbox protect the workflow.

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:48.140 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
Discord acceptance, matching receipts, and signed webhook delivery

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:52.340 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
have distinct states. A configured destination is required before

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:57.080 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
sending. Finally, download the report with its source, inputs,

00:01:57.520 --> 00:01:59.460 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
model identity, and exclusions.

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:02.160 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
Device history works without an account;

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:04.260 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
private cloud storage is optional.

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:08.240 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
The same responsive workspace runs in supported browsers as

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:09.500 line:95% position:50% size:90% align:center
an installable web app.
